icrobial infection) Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":180,"end":180,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":188,"end":188,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":193,"end":193,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ISG15)"},{"type":"Region","start":200,"end":360,"description":"Interaction with HERC5"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":237,"end":237,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":244,"end":244,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":253,"end":253,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":267,"end":289,"description":""},{"type":"Cross-link","start":360,"end":360,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ISG15)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":366,"end":366,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":366,"end":366,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ISG15)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":385,"end":385,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":386,"end":386,"description":"Diphosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":386,"end":386,"description":"Phosphoserine; by TBK1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":396,"end":396,"description":"Phosphoserine; by IKKE and TBK1"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":398,"end":398,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":404,"end":404,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":427,"end":427,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Monomer (PubMed:16846591, PubMed:16979567, PubMed:20049431, PubMed:36603579). Homodimer; phosphorylation-induced (PubMed:22394562, PubMed:25636800, PubMed:26347139, PubMed:36603579). Interacts (when phosphorylated) with CREBBP (PubMed:16154084, PubMed:27302953). Interacts with MAVS (via phosphorylated pLxIS motif) (PubMed:16153868, PubMed:25636800, PubMed:27302953). Interacts with TICAM1 (via phosphorylated pLxIS motif) (PubMed:12471095, PubMed:14739303, PubMed:25636800, PubMed:27302953). Interacts with STING1 (via phosphorylated pLxIS motif) (PubMed:22394562, PubMed:25636800, PubMed:27302953, PubMed:28331227). Interacts with STING1 (when phosphorylated at 'Ser-358'); interaction with STING1 phosphorylated at this site may promote IRF3 molecular adapter activity, leading to TRAF6 recruitment and NF-kappa-B activation (PubMed:40973797). Interacts with IKBKE and TBK1 (PubMed:16281057, PubMed:23478265, PubMed:25636800). Interacts with TICAM2 (PubMed:14517278). Interacts with RBCK1 (PubMed:18711448). Interacts with HERC5 (PubMed:20308324). Interacts with DDX3X (phosphorylated at 'Ser-102'); the interaction allows the phosphorylation and activation of IRF3 by IKBKE (PubMed:23478265, PubMed:27980081). Interacts with TRIM21 and ULK1, in the presence of TRIM21; this interaction leads to IRF3 degradation by autophagy (PubMed:18641315, PubMed:26347139). Interacts with RIOK3; RIOK3 probably mediates the interaction of TBK1 with IRF3 (PubMed:19557502). Interacts with ILRUN; the interaction inhibits IRF3 binding to its DNA consensus sequence (PubMed:29802199). Interacts with LYAR; this interaction impairs IRF3 DNA-binding activity (PubMed:31413131). Interacts with TRAF3 (PubMed:27980081). Interacts with ZDHHC11; ZDHHC11 recruits IRF3 to STING1 upon DNA virus infection and thereby promotes IRF3 activation (PubMed:28331227). Interacts with HSP90AA1; the interaction mediates IRF3 association with TOMM70 (PubMed:20628368, PubMed:25609812). Interacts with BCL2; the interaction decreases upon Sendai virus infection (PubMed:25609812). Interacts with BAX; the interaction is direct, increases upon Sendai virus infection and mediates the formation of the apoptosis complex TOMM70:HSP90AA1:IRF3:BAX (PubMed:25609812). Interacts with DDX56 (PubMed:31340999). Interacts with NBR1 (PubMed:35914352)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with rotavirus A NSP1 (via pLxIS motif); this interaction leads to the proteasome-dependent degradation of IRF3"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with herpes virus 8/HHV-8 protein VIRF1 (PubMed:11314014)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with Seneca Valley virus protease 3C; this interaction is involved in the suppression of IRF3 expression and phosphorylation by the virus"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with herpes virus 1/HHV-1 protein UL2; this interaction inhibits IRF3 phosphorylation and nuclear translocation"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with herpes virus 2/HHV-2 protein ICP27; this interaction inhibits IRF3 phosphorylation and nuclear translocation"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with human cytomegalovirus protein UL44; this interaction prevents IRF3 binding to its promoters"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with the two fragments of MERS-COV protein N produced by CASP6 through proteolytic cleavage; both interactions inhibit IRF3 nuclear translocation after activation and IFN signaling"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q14653-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":300,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000599223.5"],"refseq":["NM_001197124.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001184053.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,200],[201,328,100]],"edits":[{"start":201,"end":327,"original":"EWEFEVTAFYRGRQVFQQTISCPEGLRLVGSEVGDRTLPG","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":127,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":121,"foldedMissing":121,"features":[[10,127,0],[15,127,0],[16,1,0],[17,1,0],[18,1,0],[19,2,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q14653-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q14653-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":74,"plddt":[[0,1],[50,1],[70,3],[90,34],[70,11],[90,19],[70,6],[